## lower-bound.soar -- selection-world: 2 elaborations, 6 applications (v2.30).
## Lower bounds of evaluations (^flags.iterative-step tie-impasse, ^flags.optimize true, cost metric).
## With tie-impasse depth the depth counts nested ties, not operators: after a nested tie is decided the look-ahead goes on applying
## operators, so the value of an operator is the result of one look-ahead path whose nested choices were made on partial information.
## A success on that path is a real cost (an upper bound); a failure or failure-cutoff on it does not prove the operator worse.
## Each evaluation holds one ^lower-bound: none while no branch below it has been cut off by the depth, otherwise the lowest cost bound
## of such a branch. It starts as none and is replaced, never negated, so chunks built over it keep the test.
## The top selection (^bound-check true) lets an evaluation lose only when it is closed (Operator_Tie/elaborations.soar): its lower bound is
## none or not below the best value found. Otherwise the top tie stays, the depth is incremented, and the evaluation is evaluated again.

## ---- elaborations ----

## Elaborate lower-bound: of two bounds the higher is removed (bounds can arrive from two branches in one phase).
sp {selection-world*elaborate*evaluation*lower-bound*keep-lowest
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound { <low> <> none }
                 ^lower-bound { > <low> <high> })
-->
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound <high> -)}

## Elaborate lower-bound: none is removed once a bound has arrived.
sp {selection-world*elaborate*evaluation*lower-bound*replace-none
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound none
                 ^lower-bound <> none)
-->
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound none -)}

## ---- operator application ----

## Apply evaluate-operator -> lower-bound none (every mode). Every rule that writes a value into an evaluation tests its ^lower-bound with $,
## so the chunk built from the value tests the bound literally. A value with lower-bound none was computed with no depth cut-off below it,
## and its chunk holds at any depth. A value computed below a cut-off is learned with that bound (or not at all, when its derivation reaches
## exceed-depth, which tests ^quiescence t); its chunk never fires in a fresh evaluation, which starts with lower-bound none.
sp {selection-world*apply*evaluate-operator*lower-bound*none
   :default
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^operator <operator>)
   (<operator> ^name evaluate-operator
               ^evaluation <evaluation>)
-->
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound none)}

## Apply depth-exceeded (o-support) -> lower-bound: a depth-exceeded evaluation is bounded by its estimated total cost.
sp {selection-world*apply*evaluation*lower-bound*depth-exceeded
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^flags <flags>
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<flags> ^iterative-step tie-impasse
            ^optimize true
            ^cost-metric << unit time >>)
   (<evaluation> ^symbolic-value depth-exceeded
                 ^estimated-total-cost <bound>
                 ^lower-bound none)
-->
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound <bound>
                 ^lower-bound none -)}

## Apply depth-exceeded (o-support) -> lower-bound: a lower estimated total cost replaces a bound.
sp {selection-world*apply*evaluation*lower-bound*depth-exceeded*lower
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^flags <flags>
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<flags> ^iterative-step tie-impasse
            ^optimize true
            ^cost-metric << unit time >>)
   (<evaluation> ^symbolic-value depth-exceeded
                 ^estimated-total-cost <bound>
                 ^lower-bound { <old> > <bound> })
-->
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound <bound>
                 ^lower-bound <old> -)}

## Apply pass-up (o-support) -> lower-bound: a bound in a nested selection bounds the evaluation of the operator whose look-ahead holds it.
## None is then removed by replace-none.
sp {selection-world*apply*evaluation*lower-bound*pass-up*none
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^flags <flags>
              ^superstate.evaluation <parent>
              ^evaluation.lower-bound { <bound> <> none })
   (<flags> ^iterative-step tie-impasse
            ^optimize true
            ^cost-metric << unit time >>)
   (<parent> ^lower-bound none)
-->
   (<parent> ^lower-bound <bound>
             ^lower-bound none -)}

## Apply pass-up (o-support) -> lower-bound: a lower bound in a nested selection; the higher one is then removed by keep-lowest.
sp {selection-world*apply*evaluation*lower-bound*pass-up*lower
   :default
   :o-support
   (state <s> ^name selection
              ^flags <flags>
              ^superstate.evaluation <parent>
              ^evaluation.lower-bound { <bound> <> none })
   (<flags> ^iterative-step tie-impasse
            ^optimize true
            ^cost-metric << unit time >>)
   (<parent> ^lower-bound { <old> > <bound> })
-->
   (<parent> ^lower-bound <bound>
             ^lower-bound <old> -)}

## Apply increment-current-evaluation-depth -> removes the evaluations that are not closed; they are evaluated again at the new depth.
## The negated test is on the top selection's own evaluations and makes no result, so no chunk is built from it.
sp {selection-world*apply*increment-current-evaluation-depth*remove-open-evaluations
   :default
   (state <s> ^operator.name increment-current-evaluation-depth
              ^bound-check true
              ^evaluation <evaluation>)
   (<evaluation> ^lower-bound <> none
                -^closed true)
-->
   (<s> ^evaluation <evaluation> -)}
